---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Character from '../components/Character.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About - Jaival Shah" description="A short introduction and how I work.">
  <section class="about wrap">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>design things that make sense and look good doing it.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I'm Jaival, a Vancouver-based UI/UX designer with a background that sits
          somewhere between design, technology, and real-world problem solving. I create
          digital experiences that feel intuitive, considered, and visually sharp,
          combining user thinking with the technical curiosity to understand how things
          actually work.
        </p>

        <hr class="rule" />

        <h3>How I got here</h3>
        <p>
          I studied Interactive Arts & Technology and Publishing at SFU, where I started
          working across UI/UX, web design, visual design, and digital media. Projects
          like Senior Circle and CloveByQuantum pushed me deeper into research, user
          flows, prototyping, usability testing, and turning designs into real responsive
          websites.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the same time, working in AV and IT at SFU gave me a different perspective
          on design. I spend a lot of time watching people interact with technology in
          the real world - sometimes when everything works perfectly, and sometimes when
          one confusing button is enough to derail the whole experience. That made me
          care less about designing something that simply looks good and more about
          making things that feel obvious to use.
        </p>

        <h3>What I look for in a project</h3>
        <p>
          I like projects where there's something to untangle: a confusing flow, an
          outdated interface, too much information, or a good idea that hasn't quite
          found the right experience yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm especially drawn to digital products, websites, platforms, and interfaces
          where interaction and visual design matter equally. Give me something clunky
          and I'll probably start thinking about how I'd redesign it.
        </p>

        <h3>Outside work</h3>
        <p>
          When I'm not moving pixels around, I'm usually DJing, playing football,
          working around live events, shooting or editing something, or messing around
          with some piece of technology I probably didn't need to touch.
        </p>
        <p>
          Music and live events are a big part of my life, and I think that carries into
          my design work too - timing, energy, attention, and knowing when something
          needs more and when it needs less.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-side">
        <Character
          size={300}
          poses={{
            front: '/character/idle-front.png',
            left: '/character/three-quarter-left.png',
            right: '/character/three-quarter-right.png',
            wave: '/character/waving.png',
          }}
        />
        <dl class="fact-list">
          <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Vancouver, Canada</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Available</dt><dd>Freelance / Contract / Collaborations</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Speaks</dt><dd>English + fluent in tech jargon</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem); }
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .about-copy h1 {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    max-width: 22ch;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-optical-sizing: auto;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 96;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .about-copy .lede {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-optical-sizing: auto;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 24;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-align: justify;
  }
  .about-copy .rule {
    border: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--rule);
    margin-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }
  .about-copy h3 {
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-optical-sizing: auto;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 48;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .about-copy p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-block: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-align: justify;
    font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 1.1vw, 1rem);
  }

  .about-side {
    position: sticky;
    top: 6rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  .fact-list {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .fact-list > div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .fact-list dt {
    font-size: clamp(0.65rem, 0.8vw, 0.75rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .fact-list dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 1.1vw, 1.05rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
    .about-side { position: static; }
  }
</style>
